WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:05.304 line:0%
-Dua, one of your biggest fans
is a man named Papa Richy.

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:07.106 line:0%
All right?
He's 80 years old,

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:09.842 line:0%
and he went viral on TikTok
after his granddaughter

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:12.244 line:0%
surprised him with tickets to
your concert for his birthday.

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:14.914
His reaction got over
7 million views.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.649
This is real.
Check this out.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.486
-"Admission ticket,
Richard L. Waldorf."

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:22.956
-"And Elena Waldorf."
-"Dua Lipa in concert"?!

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:25.724
Are you [bleep] me?!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.724 --> 00:00:28.895
Are you [bleep] me?!
Really?!

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.229
Is this a real thing?
-Yeah!

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:31.563
-Holy [bleep]

00:00:31.563 --> 00:00:36.069
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.170
-Oh, it's just
such a good video.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.973
-Yeah.
-It made me so happy.

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.175
-Well, since he's such
a huge fan of yours,

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.810
we wanted to give Papa Richy
another surprise.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.512
And this is real.
It's happening right now, guys.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:47.746
We reached out to him,

00:00:47.746 --> 00:00:50.249
pretending that we were
a radio station, okay?

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:52.418
In New York, and told him
that he won a contest

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:54.620
for the number-one
TikTok video of the year.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.489
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.556
Amazing.
-He believed us.

00:00:57.556 --> 00:00:59.025
He loved it, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:01.961
So, yesterday, we flew him and
his granddaughter to New York.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:04.430
He's in our building right now
as we're talking.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.599
The TV monitors are not on
in the building.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:09.102
And he thinks he's about to be
interviewed on a radio show

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:11.537
and get a tour of "30 Rock."

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:13.573
And here he is
a few minutes ago.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.041
We have GoPro cameras.
That's his --

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.042
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.577
So he has no clue
what's going down.

00:01:18.577 --> 00:01:20.446
And, in fact, someone --

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:21.580
There was some
"Tonight Show" sign,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.082
and he said,
"Oh, I love "The Tonight Show.'"

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:24.317
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.618
So I was like, "Oh, cool.
This is gonna be great."

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.186
-Well, he's gonna --
he's gonna get the surprise...

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:28.721
-Of his life.
-...of his life.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.156
-All right, so right now,
we all need to be really quiet,

00:01:31.156 --> 00:01:33.358
'cause, seriously,
he's being led to what he thinks

00:01:33.358 --> 00:01:35.327
is the radio station.

00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:37.230
And what he doesn't know is,
he's about to walk

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.798
onto "The Tonight Show"
and meet Dua Lipa.

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:39.965
[ Laughter ]
All right?

00:01:39.965 --> 00:01:41.133
So, all right, let's get ready.
He's --

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.936
-Should I come with you?
-Yeah, you come with me.

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:46.806
We'll hear it.
We'll hear it when he's here.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.041
-Ready as
we're ever gonna be.

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:50.877
-Your first radio interview?
-First radio interview.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:53.179
-Oh, great, good.
-Papa, I will follow you.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.080
-Okay.
I'm gonna follow.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.451
-He's coming through.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.487
I think we can hear him.

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:05.091
[ Laughs ]

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:08.027
-Well, I'll follow you, Pop.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.795
-Okay.
-Okay? You first.

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:11.898
-I'm a real Jimmy Fallon fan.

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.733
-This is where Jimmy
always gets ready over here.

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.868
-Oh, my God!
Hi, Jim.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.905
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:20.907
-We'll just cut through, uh...

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:23.976
-Everyone,
please welcome Papa Richy!

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:27.914
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:30.717 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:32.318
Jimmy Fallon.
-Thank you.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.886
-I'm Jimmy Fallon.

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:35.588
You're on "The Tonight Show."

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.389
This is Dua Lipa.

00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:39.325
-Oh, my God!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.261
Holy [bleep]!

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:43.763
-Hi!
-Oh, my God!

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:44.763
Can I -- Can I shake your hand
or something?

00:02:44.763 --> 00:02:45.764
-Of course.
-Yes.

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:46.765
-Okay.
-Hello.

00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:48.668
-Your hands are freezing.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.402
-My hands actually are freezing.
-And this is your --

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:52.038
This is your granddaughter?
-Yes, I'm Katie.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.806
-Katie, how are you?
Jimmy.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:56.108
-Hi, Katie.
-It's Katie's 22nd birthday.

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:57.877
-It's Katie's birthday.
Happy birthday to you.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:58.945
-Happy birthday.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.713
-What a present
this is right here.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.115
-Yes.
-Now, I read something that said

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:06.185
that one of your dreams
is to dance with Dua Lipa.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:08.520
-Yes, yes, of course.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.623
-Can we make --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:11.657 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:13.892
Can we make that dream
a reality?

00:03:13.892 --> 00:03:16.395
Oh, my --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:20.099
-♪ Hey, hey, hey ♪

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.468
Ooh!

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.736
All right, let's --

00:03:24.736 --> 00:03:25.871
-You're supposed to be --
You're supposed to be on tour.

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:27.573
-My thanks to Dua Lipa!
-I am on tour.

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:30.509
-Papa Richy!
His granddaughter Katie!

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:32.044
Happy birthday!
Stick around!

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:34.780
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show" after the break.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:44.790 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:49.829 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.731
-We were at your first show.
-Oh, you were?

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:52.965
-In Miami.
-In Miami?

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:54.867
-Yes.
-Did you enjoy it?

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.502
-Loved it.
-I'm so happy.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:59.572
-That first outfit you had on --
that green outfit.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:00.706
-All right, all right,
come on, now.

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:03.909
[ Laughter ]
-All right, all right.

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:06.245 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.047
-I got to dance with Dua!

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.282
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:11.584 line:0%
You look fantastic.
-Thank you. Only for you.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:12.652 line:0%
-I mean, come on.

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:13.853 line:0%
-You know I always
make a big effort

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:14.853 line:0%
when I come on this show.
-You really always do.

00:04:14.853 --> 00:04:16.355 line:0%
I love it.
-I love you, bud.

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:19.358 line:0%
-You know, helped us out
when we didn't have a show --

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:21.026 line:0%
we didn't have an audience,
I was doing it in my home.

00:04:21.026 --> 00:04:22.528
-Yeah.
-And you were so cool.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:25.365
You Zoomed in to me in my home,
but I think --

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.865
I want to say
you were the first artist

00:04:26.865 --> 00:04:28.968
to make a performance, a video.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.971
-Yeah, I set up a green screen
in my living room --

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:34.306
-Yes, you made a whole video.

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:36.475
-For "The Tonight Show,"
and I just couldn't believe it.

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:38.144
I was like, "I can't believe I
have to set up a green screen

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.711
and do this.
-You were the first artist

00:04:39.711 --> 00:04:41.013
to do that.
-It was amazing.

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:42.515
-Thank you for doing that.
-It turned out so good.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:43.850
It's always kind of scary,
you know,

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.519
kind of getting in the zone
when it was so new.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.022
-Everyone kind of followed
your thing and started doing

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:51.023
what you were doing, so I can't
thank you enough for that.

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:54.026
And congrats on your
Future Nostalgia Tour.

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:56.028
Just played the Garden.
-Yes.

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:57.897
-Oh, my gosh.
The Madison Square Garden.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:58.898
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.400
Dua!
-Thank you.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.101
-What was it --
Alright, talk to me.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.103
-It was surreal.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:07.273
It really exceeded
all my expectations.

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:11.610
I think when you go to a place
like New York, you always feel

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.313
like maybe people are gonna be
a bit more critical,

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:15.581
people are gonna, like...
-Sure.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.850
-But everyone just kind of
rode the wave with me.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.018
It was amazing.
They we were all up for it.

00:05:20.018 --> 00:05:21.754
The floor was shaking.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.589
-Yeah, when that place --
-It was -- it was brilliant.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:24.924
It was brilliant. Loved it.

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.626
-When Madison Square Garden
rocks, it just rocks.

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.794
It's like this studio,
Studio 6B.

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:30.463
Here we go. This is it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:31.964
It's happening.
-Oh, the floor.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.298
-The floor shakes.
-I can feel it.

00:05:33.298 --> 00:05:35.801
-Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:38.471
-People are talking about
the tour, crazy awesome reviews.

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:39.705
Congrats.

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:42.475
They love the costumes.
They love the dancing.

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:46.479
And on social media, they're
loving one dance in particular.

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.147
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:51.450
Yeah, and I love that
you did this 'cause...

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.352
Should I explain it,
or do you want to?

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:56.689
-I mean, you can start, and then
I'll, like, riff off it.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:06:00.058
-I want to say it was like
in 2017-ish, around that time,

00:06:00.058 --> 00:06:04.230
you did a dance that people --
some haters got online

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:07.266
and said this is a lazy dance
or something, it's uninspired.

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.268
-It was kind of like,
"Oh, she looks like she's trying

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:11.070
to put her shoe on in a rush
or something."

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.204
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:12.204 --> 00:06:14.139
-Why do people just
have to be so mean?

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:15.474
-I think it's okay.

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:17.410
You know, today
when I look back on it --

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.411
and the reason I guess
why we're talking about it

00:06:19.411 --> 00:06:21.080
is 'cause I've brought it back.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.815
I'm doing it on my tour.
-Yeah.

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:26.152
-I'm reclaiming it because there
was a moment where, actually,

00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:27.486
it caused me a lot of grief.

00:06:27.486 --> 00:06:29.154
Like, I was being bullied
online.

00:06:29.154 --> 00:06:30.856
It wasn't very nice.

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:33.359
But -- But now
I'm, like, you know,

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:35.361
I can look at it
from a different perspective.

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:37.530
I look back on it
with such fondness,

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.533
'cause it helped me grow into
the artist I wanted to become.

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:44.203
It made me, like, work harder.
I went in, I did more rehearsal.

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:46.038
I just wanted to become
a real performer,

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:47.873
and I think that was kind of
the thing that I needed.

00:06:47.873 --> 00:06:50.042
-And now you open --
is it "Don't Start Now"?

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.777
-Yeah, I start
"Don't Start Now" with it.

00:06:51.777 --> 00:06:53.012
-With that dance?
-Yep.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:54.414
-And everyone goes nuts
'cause it's like,

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:56.081
"Yeah, see,
don't make fun of this.

00:06:56.081 --> 00:06:58.217
Now I'm doing this every show,
so get ready."

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:00.419
Could you show me the move?

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:03.422
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:03.422 --> 00:07:05.257
I'll do it with you.
-Will you do it with me?

00:07:05.257 --> 00:07:07.093
Someone in the audience
was like, "Yeah!"

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:09.195
-Yeah.
-Someone's really excited.

00:07:11.263 --> 00:07:13.265
I don't know if I can do it in
these boots, but you know what?

00:07:13.265 --> 00:07:15.601
Snow, boots, rain, wind, shine,
whatever.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.269
-You're Dua Lipa.
You can do anything, man.

00:07:17.269 --> 00:07:18.770
-Okay.
-Alright.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:20.105
That's it.

00:07:20.105 --> 00:07:21.774
[ Audience cheers ]

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:23.276
I can't do it.
-Yep. Come on. Come on.

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:24.610
Hip, hip, hip, hip!
-This is embarrassing.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:27.613
This is me doing it.
That is me doing it.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:30.082
That is me doing it, by the way.
So bad.

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:33.085
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:35.921
See, that almost hurt me.
That's how old I am.

00:07:35.921 --> 00:07:37.590
Oh, my God, how sad?

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.257
But I love that you did that.

00:07:39.257 --> 00:07:41.593
I love that you
put it out there.

00:07:41.593 --> 00:07:43.863
I just think you're cool.

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:46.031
I also -- I want to talk
about Elton John

00:07:46.031 --> 00:07:47.366
while I can talk to you,

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:49.768
because that was the greatest
move of all moves.

00:07:49.768 --> 00:07:51.770
"Cold Heart."
I'm like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.939
And it went to number one.
-It did.

00:07:53.939 --> 00:07:57.276
-And, wait, so what's it like
working with Sir Elton?

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:59.946
-[ Exhales sharply ] It --
I mean, I have so many --

00:07:59.946 --> 00:08:02.582
I'm so lucky to have so many
"pinch me" moments in my life.

00:08:02.582 --> 00:08:03.649
-Yeah.

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:05.450
-And that's definitely
a massive one.

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:07.786
He's somebody I've looked up to
my whole life.

00:08:07.786 --> 00:08:11.023
So to get to do
the song together,

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:13.359
to re-create his iconic songs --

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:16.061
-You crushed it, though.
-It's just a massive honor.

00:08:16.061 --> 00:08:17.262
I'm so grateful.
And I get to perform it.

00:08:17.262 --> 00:08:18.764
-And adding "Rocket Man"
in there, too.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:20.433
Like, yo! So good!

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:22.768
-It's just amazing, and I get to
perform it night after night.

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:24.770
And it's just --
it's a dream come true.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.539
I really -- in that moment,

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:28.541
I really just kind of
soak it all up

00:08:28.541 --> 00:08:31.543
and I can't believe everything
that's happening to me.

00:08:31.543 --> 00:08:35.547
-And then he gave you a very
nice gift, a memorable gift.

00:08:35.547 --> 00:08:39.719
-He did give me a very lovely,
memorable gift.

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:41.887
Sir Elton John put a ring on it.

00:08:41.887 --> 00:08:43.222
-He put --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:44.557
-[ Laughs ] I'm joking.

00:08:44.557 --> 00:08:46.158
-You're marrying --
-Before this gets into the press

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:47.493
or whatever --
-You married Elton John?

00:08:47.493 --> 00:08:48.660
-No, I didn't.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:50.162
I didn't, I didn't, I didn't.
-Oh, okay.

00:08:50.162 --> 00:08:52.131
-I think David would fight me.

00:08:52.131 --> 00:08:53.632
-Yeah, he would. Of course.
-For sure.

00:08:53.632 --> 00:08:59.972
-But he gave me a very beautiful
ring that belonged to him,

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:03.475
as just kind of, like, a token

00:09:03.475 --> 00:09:05.811
when we performed together
for the first time.

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.813
And it was just -- I was just --

00:09:07.813 --> 00:09:09.315
-How cool is that?
-Yeah.

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:10.983
I keep it...
-I love Elton John.

00:09:10.983 --> 00:09:13.118
-I actually kept it at home
locked up in a safe

00:09:13.118 --> 00:09:14.954
'cause I just don't think
it was safe back here.

00:09:14.954 --> 00:09:16.956
-No, not on our show.
No, no, no, no.

00:09:16.956 --> 00:09:19.124
[ Laughter ]
I'm famous for this.

00:09:19.124 --> 00:09:20.959
I want to talk about --
you're always, again,

00:09:20.959 --> 00:09:22.794
doing something new
and different.

